A||N||10||Seanh||Smoke and Gas Smell?||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||05-29-2001||09:49 PM||||Ever since I got my 87 GT 2.8 Auto, its seems to smoke some white smoke on start-up, sometimes even after its still warm. Iv notice some long cranking time occasionally, but not always. Today, me and a friend were reving the engine and I noticed it smokes when I rev it, and step on it from a stop. It also has a gas smell when I rev it up, don't know about driving cuz I can't smell it. The car seems to run ok, its idle is a little ruff, but never dies or anything. The timeing is perfect also. Iv also noticed some pretty lousy gas milage, 18mpg at the most in town. Any guesses on whats wrong? It starting to get me concerned, like maybe the engine is running rich or somthing. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||05-29-2001||11:23 PM||||A lot of what you are concerned about sounds like a normal 16 year old engine.<P>White smoke is usually caused by coolant, are you loosing any from your reservoir and don't have and external leak.  OR are you just seeing a puff of oil smoke on start up and rev up from an older engine. <P>I have been fighting with intermittent extended crank-not cured it but is a lot better after replacing badly corroded ignition module and pickup coil.<P>If you are smelling a raw gas odor you must have a fuel leak. Look into this, it may be as simple as a fuel cap seal.  or fuel line rotten.||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||05-29-2001||11:53 PM||||it could be as simple as a bad O2 sensor or as complex as a sticky injector. If you haven't changed your O2 sensor you should start there.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>                <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/3GTS_SIG.gif">                 </A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||05-30-2001||12:11 AM||||This engine has new head gaskets, and all gaskets up from there. I have recently replaced the O2 sensor, about 3 weeks ago. I am not looseing any coolant, nor having any air in the cooling system problems. Could be the puff of oil you are talking about, but I am not totally sure. Ignition coil and modual are new. I was broke, and they needed replacement so I got the GP Sorensen crap from Advance, and already had the module fail, so I put the old one back in and it works fine now. I did notice a nice increase in lost power from replacing the coil, old one much have been dieing slowly. Could perhaps be a fuel leak, but I don't think so. I have replaced the gas cap in trying to solve this situation with no help. Could these problems be a bad fuel vapor canister perhaps? Sticky injector is good possibility, but I don't know how I would check this without just haveing them blueprinted.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||05-30-2001||10:05 AM||||The startup smoke sounds allot like valve guides. the run smoke could be valves and/or rings.<P>You need to do both dry and wet compression testing. Low compression will kill milage just as sure as anything else.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ken Wittlief||05-30-2001||10:11 AM||||putting a bottle of Gunkout injector cleaner through the gas tank wont hurt - if your injectors are mildly dirty it will help clean up the spray pattern. If gas is sputtering from the injectors instead of spraying in a nice mist then it wont burn as well and will screw up the mixture.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ken Wittlief||05-30-2001||10:13 AM||||IF you are getting 18mpg city your not doing too bad - tank up this weekend and hit the highway for a hundred miles or so and see what your highway mileage is - should be 25 or so (Good excuse to take a cruise in your fiero - not that we ever need an excuse).<P>  If you are getting 18mpg or worst highway then you would have reason to suspect something is wrong back there.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Ken Wittlief||05-30-2001||10:16 AM||||also ive noticed if I top my gas tank off I get a raw gas smell inside my fiero (like I spilled gas on my sneakers) - I dont know what it is on my car - i suspect a vapor line to the tank or the seal on the the fuel pump.<P>  do you only notice the gas smell after you tank up? Is it raw gas or is it like driving behind an old ford truck (rich exhaust smell)?||||reg||1
Z||000008||saleenfiero||05-30-2001||05:01 PM||||Vapor canister anyone?||||reg||1
Z||000009||Seanh||05-30-2001||06:23 PM||||Its definatly a rich running smell, not a raw gas smell. I don't smell it inside the car either. I know my injectors are in pretty bad condition, so I am getting a set with less then 30K on them and going to swap to see if it makes an improvment. I haven't messed with any wet compression, but dry compression came to be about 120 psi, not much off for each cylinder. I might just pull a plug real quick and check again, just to be sure. Let me do that, and I'll get back to ya in a couple minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000010||PBJ||05-30-2001||08:37 PM||||All three of my v6 fiero's have had a run rich smell to them especially cold. but put them on the dyno for emissions test and every one says they will fail and they all passed.  I think the rich odor is normal, My 2.8's in a celebrity I had were the same.||||reg||1
